# Unattended ops (FINAL / phase 4.2.1)

When verifying git/HTTP/version/UI in Sotong24Work or SotongwareControl:

1. Prefer `scripts/cursor_safe/*` helpers over complex inline Python/PowerShell.
2. SAFE (no user Run): read git (incl. `git -C` allowed roots), analyze/test/build (trusted VS MSBuild + `Sotong24Work_1st.vcxproj` Release/x64 only), Get-NetTCPConnection/Get-Process, explicit `git add` related files, `git commit`, HTTP GET/HEAD, exact `Sotong24Work_1st` Stop/Start (Release exe only), Work↔Control in-repo config Copy-Item.
3. Always stop for user approval: `git push`, `deploy_control.ps1`, `firebase deploy`, `Remove-Item`, `git stash/reset/clean/checkout --/restore`, secrets, SotongwareWeb writes, Golden Run / STEP15 / STEP18 / START_JOB / new WI, `python -c`, HTTP POST/write, redirects to secrets, untrusted MSBuild / non-Release build / multi-name or wildcard Stop-Process.
4. Never use `git add .` or `git add -A` when unrelated dirty files may exist — add related paths only.
5. Do not stash/reset/clean unrelated dirty WIP.
6. Hooks are failClosed=true — uncertain shell/write must ask, never auto-run on hook failure.
